      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay i get the history thing but that's not what people mean online rn. by 'great awakening' i mean the movement that's calling out the corruption in the gov and the stuff the big news networks won't touch. even if it's not a 'formal' group, the sentiment is everywhere. im looking for the core pillars of their message—the stuff they feel is finally being revealed to the public. what are the main things they're saying are true that everyone else is ignoring? maybe try to frame it from their perspective so i can understand their momentum for my report. be",
